ary":"A locally operated lunch counter gives the Oak Street block a specific daytime purpose.","evidence_claim":"Cross Creek Sandwich Shop is located at 1003 Oak Street and serves breakfast on Saturday plus lunch Monday through Saturday.","source_url":"https://www.crosscreeksandwichshop.com/contact","source_title":"Cross Creek Sandwich Shop | Contact | Conway, AR","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cross%20Creek%20Sandwich%20Shop%201003%20Oak%20Street%20Conway%20AR","access_notes":"Posted hours are 11 a.m.–2 p.m. Monday–Friday and 8–10:30 a.m. plus 11 a.m.–2 p.m. Saturday.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"rogers-plaza-oak-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Rogers Plaza","title":"Start the Tiny Toads Tour","subtitle":"Oak Street — Downtown Conway","notes":"Use Rogers Plaza as the Oak Street starting point for the city’s Tiny Toads public-art route, then follow the numbered downtown stops.","short_summary":"The gateway plaza supplies a documented starting point for a self-guided art walk.","evidence_claim":"Conway’s official Tiny Toads Tour identifies Rogers Plaza at 920 Oak Street as stop 1 and the gateway to Downtown Conway.","source_url":"https://maps.conwayarkansas.gov/documents/publicart/TinyToadsTour.pdf","source_title":"Tiny Toads Tour","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-03-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rogers%20Plaza%20920%20Oak%20Street%20Conway%20AR","access_notes":"The city’s downloadable tour map presents Rogers Plaza as an outdoor route stop.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"faulkner-county-museum-locust-avenue","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Faulkner County Museum","title":"Read the County Through Its Collections","subtitle":"Locust Avenue — Courthouse Square","notes":"Turn onto Locust Avenue to examine regional objects, photographs, art, and archival materials inside the historic 1896 county jail.","short_summary":"A former jail now holds the county’s material and documentary history.","evidence_claim":"The Faulkner County Museum at 801 Locust Avenue occupies the historic 1896 jail and maintains historical, archival, art, image, and object collections.","source_url":"https://www.faulknercountyar.gov/museum/","source_title":"Museum – Faulkner County Government","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Faulkner%20County%20Museum%20801%20Locust%20Ave%20Conway%20AR","access_notes":"The museum lists public hours of 9 a.m.–4 p.m. Monday through Thursday and recommends calling for information.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"conway-city-hall-main-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Conway City Hall","title":"See Local Government in Session","subtitle":"Main Street — Downtown Conway","notes":"Use the Main Street block for an open City Council meeting; verify the current agenda before entering the second-floor chambers.","short_summary":"City Hall offers a concrete civic reason to visit Main Street on meeting nights.","evidence_claim":"Conway City Council meetings are open to the public and ordinarily occur at 6 p.m. on the second and fourth Tuesdays at 1111 Main Street.","source_url":"https://www.conwayarkansas.gov/meetings/","source_title":"Meetings – City of Conway, Arkansas","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Conway%20City%20Hall%201111%20Main%20Street%20Conway%20AR","access_notes":"Check the city meeting page for res